- Criteria scores: brief match 3, silhouette 3.5, proportion and appeal 3.5, shape language 3, value and colour 4,
  materials 4, detail hierarchy 3.5, technical quality 4, game readiness 4, readability at 128 px 3.5.

## Item 5: paint-splash (commit d6e0414e) - 6.5, FAIL

Book row (line 216): 'three big round splashes in a row: red, blue, yellow'.

- Preset renders: out/paint-splash/render.png (red), render.blue.png, and render.yellow.png differ in colour: saturated
  red, blue, and yellow. This part of the brief is met.
- The shape is a thick disc with 7 lobes and 3 droplets on necks (0.289 x 0.251 x 0.04 m). It reads as a scalloped
  badge more than as wet paint.
- Defects: (1) the foot box is 0.04 m deep in 0.025 m paint, so it shows as a rectangular tab on the front and the back
  (assets/paint-splash.ts:92-93); (2) each lobe leaves a ring on the face (smoothUnion k 0.004, line 72), and the
  studio light turns the rings into bubble-like highlights in the front cutout; (3) one flat mid-value colour, and the
  front cutout mean #f3635c (pale coral) against the preset #d9443a; (4) a 0.04 m slab from the side.
- Criteria scores: brief match 4, silhouette 3, proportion and appeal 3, shape language 3, value and colour 3,
  materials 3, detail hierarchy 3, technical quality 3, game readiness 4, readability at 128 px 3.5. The mean gives 6.5.
- Pipeline gap (N3, outside this step): a stage prop has no colour or preset field, and only the red cutouts exist, so a
  scene places three red splashes today.
- Suggested change for the maker: foot no deeper than 0.025 m or inside the paint; lobe join k 0.02 to 0.03; a darker
  rim or vertex shade for value; rebuild the GLB, the cutouts, and the card.

## Item 6: duck, F1 and F2 (commit f098d5b9) - re-rated 7.5, pass

- F1 (wings flat, no part more than 8 mm out): pass. I measured the built GLB. For each vertex of the coverts (282) and
  the flight (147) meshes I cast a ray along -X against the body mesh (2452 triangles). The worst protrusion is
  3.67 mm (coverts) and 3.32 mm (flight); the 95th percentile is 2.8 mm. The maker measured 5.8 mm with
  wing-probe.ts. The earlier pose stood 34 mm out. In the front cutout, the 128 px sprite S, and the back view, the
  wings no longer read as arms or fins. They show as a faint fold on the flank.
- F2 (one small glint per eye, sphere 0.0025 m): pass. assets/duck.ts:80 sets glint 0 and line 121 sets the sphere
  radius. The enlarged front cutout shows a black eye with one small white dot and no second highlight.
- Rating again: 7.5 (was 7.0). The largest earlier difference is fixed. Remaining differences are small: the wings
  are almost invisible and the pale wing edge does not show, the tail fan is a grey scalloped crescent in the back
  view, the jaw bone has no geometry, the walk is small and stiff (N6). Criteria scores: brief match 4, silhouette 4,
  proportion and appeal 4, shape language 3.5, value and colour 4, materials 3.5, detail hierarchy 4, technical
  quality 3.5, game readiness 4, readability at 128 px 4, motion 3.5 (unchanged clip).
- briefs/duck.md keeps a stale wing bullet (N7).

